APPENDIX C — VLAN ISOLATION GUIDE (Ubiquiti UniFi + OPNsense)

Defense in Depth per §10.3. Zero trust between IoT and LAN.

Network Design

VLAN ID Name Subnet Purpose
10 MAIN_LAN 192.168.10.0/24 Trusted devices (phones, laptops)
20 IOT 192.168.20.0/24 HA hub, Zigbee, Voice PE, plugs, sensors
30 GUEST 192.168.30.0/24 Isolated guests
99 MGMT 192.168.99.0/24 OPNsense + UniFi controller

Key principle: IoT can only talk to the HA hub. HA hub can talk to MAIN_LAN. Nothing talks to the internet (except OPNsense itself).

OPNsense Setup Summary

1. VLANs & Interfaces: Create VLANs 10,20,30,99 on your LAN parent, assign them, set static IPv4 (e.g. 192.168.20.1/24 for IOT).
2. DHCP: Serve IOT subnet with no public DNS — set DNS server to 192.168.20.1 (the firewall itself). Set static leases: HA hub at 192.168.20.10, Voice PE at .20.
3. Firewall Rules for IOT (VLAN 20):
   · Pass HA hub to MAIN_LAN on ports 8123, 2586.
   · Pass IoT devices to HA hub (MQTT, Z2M, Assist).
   · Pass DNS and NTP only to firewall.
   · Block IoT to all other RFC1918.
   · Block IoT to WAN (the absolute kill‑switch).
4. Firewall Rules for MAIN_LAN: Allow to internet but block direct access to IoT VLAN (except to the HA hub).
5. IPv6: Disable on WAN and IOT VLAN; disable system‑wide to prevent Thread/Matter leaks (§10.2).
6. Unbound DNS: Use root hints, no upstream forwarding.

UniFi Setup Summary

1. Networks: Create VLAN‑only networks for each VLAN (DHCP handled by OPNsense).
2. Wi‑Fi: Create separate SSIDs “MyHome” (VLAN 10) and “MyHome‑IOT” (VLAN 20). Enable Client Device Isolation on the IoT SSID to prevent bulbs talking to each other.
3. Port Profiles: Assign wired IoT devices (HA Green, Voice PE) to the IOT native network.

Verification

· From HA (192.168.20.10): ping 8.8.8.8 → must fail.
· From laptop on MAIN_LAN: ping 192.168.20.21 (a bulb) → must fail.
· From HA: ping 192.168.10.50 (a laptop) → must succeed (notifications work).
· Run the Wireshark one‑liner: zero packets leaving the LAN.

