## E.1 Aqara Firmware — Version Identification & Automation

### E.1.1 Check Current Firmware Version in Zigbee2MQTT

Once paired, each device exposes its `date_code` and `software_build_id`. Use the following to audit your devices without touching a cloud hub.

**Manual inspection (Home Assistant)**  
- Developer Tools → States → Filter by `zigbee2mqtt` → Look for `software_build_id` and `date_code` attributes.

**Scripted check (MQTT command line)**  
```bash
# List all Aqara devices and their firmware versions
mosquitto_sub -h localhost -t "zigbee2mqtt/+/+" -v --pretty | \
  jq 'select(.definition.vendor=="Aqara") | {friendly_name, software_build_id, date_code}'
```

Known good Aqara firmware thresholds (as of mid‑2026):

| Model | Friendly name pattern | Minimum recommended `date_code` / `software_build_id` |
|-------|----------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|
| WSDCGQ11LM (Temp/Hum) | `sensor.*aqara` | `20230512` or later |
| MCCGQ11LM (Door/Window) | `binary_sensor.*aqara` | `20221215` or later |
| RTCGQ11LM (Motion) | `binary_sensor.*aqara_motion` | `20231101` or later |

If your device is below the threshold, proceed with the disposable‑hub update.

### E.1.2 Automating the Disposable‑Hub Update (Script)

While the physical steps must be manual, you can reduce the cloud‑footprint window. This script (run on a separate Raspberry Pi or laptop on the isolated guest network) captures the exact time your burner account exists and prompts you when to delete it.

```bash
#!/bin/bash
# aqara-disposable-update.sh
# Connect a burner Pi/laptop to the GUEST_VLAN (internet only, no LAN access).
# The script reminds you to kill the burner account after 30 minutes.

echo "Connect the Aqara hub to the guest network now."
read -p "Enter burner email used for Aqara account: " BURNER_EMAIL
START_TIME=$(date +%s)
echo "Update started at $(date). You have 30 minutes."
echo "After the app shows firmware updated, factory reset the sensor, then press Ctrl+C."

# This loop just nags you to delete the account
while true; do
  CURRENT_TIME=$(date +%s)
  ELAPSED=$(( (CURRENT_TIME - START_TIME) / 60 ))
  if [ $ELAPSED -ge 30 ]; then
    echo "⏰ 30 minutes elapsed. Delete the burner account NOW: https://account.aqara.com"
    break
  fi
  sleep 300
done
```

**Post‑cleanup:** After factory reset, pair the sensor back to your private Zigbee2MQTT and verify the new `date_code` appears via the MQTT check above.

