## E.3 LLM Performance Tuning — Commands & Metrics

### E.3.1 Model Speed Benchmarking

Always measure tokens per second with a realistic prompt that includes your entity list. Use the actual Home Assistant entity dump for an honest benchmark.

```bash
# Generate the entity list from HA API
ENTITIES=$(curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_LONG_LIVED_TOKEN" \
  http://localhost:8123/api/states | jq '[.[] | .entity_id] | tojson')

# Benchmark TinyLlama with a typical smart home query
ollama run tinyllama:1.1b --verbose <<EOF
[INST] You control a smart home. Available entities: $ENTITIES
Turn off all lights in the living room [/INST]
EOF
```

Note the `eval_count` and `eval_duration` at the end of the Ollama output. `tokens/s = eval_count / (eval_duration / 1e9)`.

### E.3.2 Setting Context Limits in Ollama

Create a custom model file with tightened constraints:

```
FROM tinyllama:1.1b
PARAMETER num_ctx 1024
PARAMETER num_predict 64
PARAMETER stop "<|im_end|>"
PARAMETER stop "</s>"
SYSTEM "You are a concise smart home controller. Respond with a JSON service call or a 1‑sentence answer. No chit‑chat. Available entities: %%ENTITIES%%"
```

Replace `%%ENTITIES%%` dynamically each time you rebuild the model (or use a template that Ollama fills from your HA integration). You can create a weekly cron job to rebuild the model with fresh entities:

```bash
#!/bin/bash
# update-home-model.sh
ENTITIES=$(curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $HA_TOKEN" \
  http://localhost:8123/api/states | jq '[.[] | select(.entity_id|test("^(light|switch|climate|lock|script)")) | .entity_id] | tojson')
  
cp /opt/ollama/modelfiles/home-base.Modelfile /tmp/home-live.Modelfile
sed -i "s|%%ENTITIES%%|$ENTITIES|g" /tmp/home-live.Modelfile
ollama create home-live -f /tmp/home-live.Modelfile
```

### E.3.3 Checking if the Hailo‑8L is Worth It

If you have a Hailo‑8L connected, first verify it’s detected:

```bash
hailortcli fw-control identify
# Should return firmware version and device ID
```

Currently, running Ollama on Hailo is experimental. A quicker win is to use the Hailo‑8L for **whisper** (speech‑to‑text) via the `hailo-whisper` project, offloading STT from the CPU and freeing up CPU for the LLM. This can cut total latency by 30‑40% even without accelerating the LLM itself.

```bash
# Install hailo-whisper (community project)
pip install hailo-whisper
hailo-whisper --model small --input "test.wav"
```

Then configure the Home Assistant `whisper` integration to use the `hailo-whisper` command‑line tool.

